# Cloudflare Pages custom response headers.
#
# Content-hashed files are immutable: their filename encodes their content,
# so they can be cached forever. Cache-Control with `immutable` prevents the
# browser from even revalidating.
#
# Vite emits built assets under /assets/*, and TanStack Start's
# staticFunctionMiddleware writes prerendered server-function responses under
# /__tsr/staticServerFnCache/ (filename = SHA-1 of the request payload). Both
# are content-addressed and safe to cache indefinitely.
#
# NOTE: there is deliberately no `/*` rule here. Cloudflare Pages already
# serves HTML with `Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` by
# default, and a broad `/*` rule would overlap these asset rules. Cloudflare
# merges all matching rules (rather than first-match), so `/*` would override
# the immutable directive below on asset requests. Keeping the rules
# non-overlapping lets the immutable caching actually take effect.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/__tsr/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
